# Only Camada's own API leaves the shared library. One pattern per line,
# without the Mach-O leading underscore; camada_exported_symbols_flag turns
# this into a version script on ELF and an exported-symbols list on Apple.
#
# The shared library statically absorbs the backends it links (CVC5, Bitwuzla,
# STP, MathSAT) and, with them, their GMP and CaDiCaL. Exporting those makes
# libcamada a provider of symbols it does not own: a process that also loads a
# real libgmp, or the Yices shared library, then has several definitions of
# __gmpz_init and friends, and the loader picks one by load order. They agree
# today only because every copy happens to be GMP 6.3.0.
#
# Camada's C++ API.
*camada*
# Typeinfo and vtables for the public classes, which a consumer needs in order
# to derive from SMTSolver or catch a Camada exception across the library
# boundary.
_ZTIN6camada*
_ZTSN6camada*
_ZTVN6camada*
